  "summary": "Pflugerville City Council approved on first reading an ordinance placing 14 proposed charter amendments on the November 2026 ballot. Among them, Proposition B would require the council to adopt rules protecting resident privacy when the city uses data, facial recognition, surveillance tools and AI, and would mandate a public approval process before deploying such technologies.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Proposition B: Requires the City Council to adopt rules that protect residents' privacy when the city collects and uses data, facial recognition, surveillance tools and artificial intelligence. It also requires a public approval process before these technologies are used and establishes standards for their responsible use.",
